WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
Put electrodes on someone's skin, and
you can record the electrical activity of

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:06.260
their heart as it beats.

3
00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:08.900
The trace is an ECG.

4
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.580
Each tall spike marks a heartbeat.

5
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:16.870
At 75 beats a minute, the
spikes come 0.8 seconds apart.

6
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.430
Now imagine cutting every
nerve that reaches a heart.

7
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.580
The spikes keep on coming.

8
00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.750
So what are those nerves for?

9
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.100
In this mission, you'll find out
where each heartbeat really begins.

10
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.360
Then you'll follow a wave of electrical
excitation as it crosses the heart's chambers.

11
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:38.690
Your mission: find out what the
nerves to your heart are really for.
